.TH SIGPROCMASK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sigprocmask \- change or inspect a signal mask
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.B int sigprocmask(int how, const sigset_t* set, sigset_t* previous);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes the calling thread's signal mask with SIG_BLOCK, SIG_UNBLOCK or
SIG_SETMASK. If set is NULL, only the previous mask is queried and how is
ignored. A non\-NULL previous receives the old mask. SIGKILL and SIGSTOP
cannot be blocked.
.PP
Crunch sigset_t is an eight\-byte Linux x86\-64 kernel mask, not libc's
sigset_t. Signal n corresponds to bit n\-1; use sigemptyset to clear it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigaction (3crunch),
.BR sigemptyset (3crunch),
.BR sigprocmask (2)
